# Sysible Server — force the virtual-GPU DRM/KMS drivers into the initramfs so
# the framebuffer console comes up EARLY, in the VM's display window, on the
# installed system.
#
# Why this is the fix for the "black screen + mouse pointer after GRUB":
# the graphical installer renders fine on the same VM because its initrd already
# carries these drivers and brings up KMS early; the installed system was going
# black because its console had no early KMS driver to light the display. Listing
# them here (with modeset on — we do NOT pass nomodeset) makes update-initramfs
# bake them in, so the display lights up immediately, matching the installer.
#
# Covers every common hypervisor GPU: VMware SVGA II (vmwgfx, amd64 Fusion),
# virtio-gpu (arm64 Fusion / QEMU/KVM), VirtualBox/QEMU std VGA (bochs-drm),
# and QXL (qxl). Harmless where a driver's device is absent — the module just
# doesn't bind.
vmwgfx
virtio-gpu
virtio_gpu
bochs-drm
bochs
qxl
